theory.intro:
**Cosecant**, **secant** and **cotangent** are the reciprocals of sine, cosine and tangent. In a right-angled triangle they are $\dfrac{\text{hyp}}{\text{opp}}$, $\dfrac{\text{hyp}}{\text{adj}}$ and $\dfrac{\text{adj}}{\text{opp}}$. On a circle of radius $r$ they use the coordinates of $P(x,y)$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes,calc}
\coordinate (A) at (0,3);
\coordinate (B) at (0,0);
\coordinate (C) at (4,0);
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,left] {opp};
\draw (B)--(C) node[midway,below] {adj};
\draw (C)--(A) node[midway,above right] {hyp};
\coordinate (ra1) at ($(B)!0.3cm!(A)$);
\coordinate (ra2) at ($(B)!0.3cm!(C)$);
\draw (ra1)--($(ra1)+(ra2)-(B)$)--(ra2);
\pic[draw,"$\theta$",angle radius=0.7cm,angle eccentricity=1.6] {angle=A--C--B};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes,calc}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P) at (2,1.5);
\coordinate (F) at (2,0);
\coordinate (X) at (3,0);
\draw[-{Stealth}] (-3.2,0)--(3.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0,-3.2)--(0,3.2) node[above] {$y$};
\draw (O) circle (2.5);
\draw (O)--(P) node[pos=0.65,above left] {$r$};
\draw[dashed] (P)--(F);
\coordinate (rb1) at ($(F)!0.25cm!(P)$);
\coordinate (rb2) at ($(F)!0.25cm!(O)$);
\draw (rb1)--($(rb1)+(rb2)-(F)$)--(rb2);
\pic[draw,"$\theta$",angle radius=0.8cm,angle eccentricity=1.7] {angle=X--O--P};
\node[above right] at (P) {$P(x,y)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.question_text:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,3);
\coordinate (B) at (0,0);
\coordinate (C) at (4,0);
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,left] {$3$};
\draw (B)--(C) node[midway,below] {$4$};
\draw (C)--(A) node[midway,above right] {$5$};
\coordinate (ra1) at ($(B)!0.3cm!(A)$);
\coordinate (ra2) at ($(B)!0.3cm!(C)$);
\draw (ra1)--($(ra1)+(ra2)-(B)$)--(ra2);
\pic[draw,"$\theta$",angle radius=0.7cm,angle eccentricity=1.6] {angle=A--C--B};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
In the right-angled triangle shown, find the exact values of $\sec\theta$, $\operatorname{cosec}\theta$, and $\cot\theta$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,4.8);
\coordinate (B) at (0,0);
\coordinate (C) at (2.0,0);
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,left] {$12$};
\draw (B)--(C) node[midway,below] {$5$};
\draw (C)--(A) node[midway,above right] {$13$};
\coordinate (ra1) at ($(B)!0.3cm!(A)$);
\coordinate (ra2) at ($(B)!0.3cm!(C)$);
\draw (ra1)--($(ra1)+(ra2)-(B)$)--(ra2);
\pic[draw,"$\alpha$",angle radius=0.8cm,angle eccentricity=1.6] {angle=A--C--B};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
In the right-angled triangle shown, find the exact value of $\cot\alpha$.
